# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.11 — THE PAGE IS DESTROYED AND ITS CONTENT IS NOT
# A page's blocks are deliberately NOT archived with it (ADR-053 §3.1), so a hard delete of the page
# row alone leaves the authored text — and its `vt_*` vault tokens — in rows no read can reach. The
# purge destroys them in the SAME transaction. This patch skips that cascade: the trash empties, the
# audit row is written, every visible assertion passes, and the tenant's content is still at rest.
#
# Aimed at the BLOCK CASCADE only. The archive-first guard, the policy, the audit, the page destroy
# and the SUBTREE cascade (3.13) are untouched.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_trash_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an admin empties a page
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/writes.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notes/writes.ex
@@ -850,7 +850,6 @@
   # One page's rows: both link directions, then its blocks, then the page itself.
   defp purge_row(mount, scope, doc) do
     with {:ok, _links} <- destroy_page_links(mount, scope, doc.id),
-         :ok <- purge_blocks(mount, scope, doc.id),
          {:ok, purged} <-
            doc
            |> Ash.Changeset.for_destroy(:purge, %{}, scope: scope)
